pport"}, {"trace_id": "step_32", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Every listed node participates in exactly one static triangle, so time-ignorant closure is present by construction. However, temporal bucketing of each triad shows its events spread over many thousands of time units, and direct edge probes inside the locally densest 1000-unit buckets find zero triangle-closing interactions there. The apparent closures are artifacts of aggregating over the full 12k window; no closing edge follows its supporting wedge within 800 units. Node activity is low and unrelated to the top-active hubs, so volume/popularity explanations are excluded."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Static structure exists, but timing does not support it.**\n\n- The window is large (3501 events, 1751 active nodes) yet the target nodes are all very low-degree (2\u20136 events each, repeat ratio \u22480.01), so background volume is not driving anything (step_01, step_03).\n- Each target node sits in exactly one static triangle (12 triangles total, one per node) \u2014 an \"ignore-time\" connection exists for every one of them (step_04). The 1-hop subgraphs make these triads explicit: 39\u201385\u20131970, 54\u2013620\u20131388, 82\u20131064\u20131467, 115\u20131303\u20131992, 116\u2013229\u20131719, 118\u2013873\u20131370, 172\u20131414\u20131634, 188\u2013731\u2013748, 207\u2013841\u20131585, 260\u20131095\u20131806 (steps 05\u201314).\n- Bucketing each triad into 1000-unit sub-windows (steps 15\u201324) shows the triad members' events scattered across the whole 12k span, never concentrating three events into any single \u2264800-unit span. E.g. triad 39/85/1970 spans buckets from 49332 to 59332; 207/841/1585 spans 47332 to 59332.\n- Direct probes of the closing edges inside the densest bucket for several triads return **no** interactions at all: 39\u201385, 39\u20131970, 85\u20131970 in [49332,50332] (steps 25\u201327); 207\u2013841, 207\u20131585, 841\u20131585 in [58332,59332] (steps 28\u201330); 116\u2013229, 229\u20131719 in [58332,59332] (steps 31\u201332). The local activity in those buckets came from other partners, not from the triangle-closing edges \u2014 the confounder \"these nodes were busy then\" is ruled out.\n\nThe triangles are therefore assembled from temporally scattered edges; no closing interaction follows its supporting wedge within 800 time units.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_6173b637\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"closure_wave\",\n  \"entities\": [39, 54, 82, 85, 115, 116, 118, 172, 188, 207, 229, 260, 1970, 1719, 841, 1585],\n  \"window\": [47332, 59332],\n  \"confidence\": 0.82,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_25\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_26\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_27\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_28\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_29\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_30\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_31\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_32\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Every listed node participates in exactly one static triangle, so time-ignorant closure is present by construction. However, temporal bucketing of each triad shows its events spread over many thousands of time units, and direct edge probes inside the locally densest 1000-unit buckets find zero triangle-closing interactions there. The apparent closures are artifacts of aggregating over the full 12k window; no closing edge follows its supporting wedge within 800 units. Node activity is low and unrelated to the top-active hubs, so volume/popularity explanations are excluded.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 55236, "total_output_tokens": 10751, "total_tokens": 65987, "total_latency_ms": 136526, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}